# red.fk: red science from plates the robots bring, into labs. Plot 30x30. Two input chests, a gear
# row, a science row taking gears and copper on two belts, the labs at the end; every row's head
# is at x = 8, so the router has columns 0..7. Shows: `assert INST.rate >= R`.
# Run:  fk rates red.fk    fk build --to report_checks
# Expect: `PASS red.rate >= 9/min: 18.000/min`; `could-pair net copp and gear` (left as two belts
# here); `red: 4 nets: 4 connected, 0 open, 0 unrouted`.
iron   = Chest<requester, item=iron-plate, rate=1/s>   @(2, 2)
copper = Chest<requester, item=copper-plate, rate=1/s> @(2, 12)
gears  = AsmRow<n=1, recipe=iron-gear-wheel>          @(8, 2)
red    = AsmRow<n=3, recipe=automation-science-pack>  @(8, 12)
labs   = LabRow<n=3>                                  @(8, 23)

net plates: iron -> gears
net copp:   copper -> red
net gear:   gears -> red
net packs:  red -> labs

assert red.rate >= 9/min
